PostalCodeValidator
===================

Strict validation for postal and ZIP codes.

Installation
============

Add the gem to your Gemfile:

  gem "validation_kit"

Usage
=====

class Person < ActiveRecord::Base
  validates :postal_code, postal_code: { country: "CA", set: true }, allow_blank: true
end

There are three ways to specify the country. Country codes are
case-insensitive ("CA", "ca", or :CA).

 (1) Pass the country code as a string:

  validates :postal_code, postal_code: { country: "CA" }

 (2) Pass the name of a method on your model that returns the country code:

  validates :postal_code, postal_code: { country: :billing_country }

 (3) Leave it out, and the validator calls your model's country method:

  validates :postal_code, postal_code: true

Validation is skipped when the country isn't supported.

Options
=======

  set: true       Reformat the stored value: Canadian and UK codes get a space
                  (K1A 0B1, SW1A 1AA) and US ZIP+4 codes a hyphen (10001-1234).
  message: "..."  A custom error message. Otherwise the standard :invalid
                  error is added; translate it with
                  activerecord.errors.models.person.attributes.postal_code.invalid.

Supported countries are Canada (CA), the United States (US), the United
Kingdom (UK or GB), Australia (AU), and New Zealand (NZ).


